legend bottom
  <b>Threading and callbacks (verified in source)</b>
  • ClientConnection.connect(...) starts one virtual thread that reads lines and calls onMessage.accept(...);
     ChatClientApp passes this::handleServerMessage and uses Platform.runLater(...) to update the UI.
  • ChatServer.start() binds a ServerSocket to config host:port, loops on accept(), and handles each Socket
     in its own virtual thread (handleClient).
  • ServerDashboard runs ChatServer.start() in a virtual thread inside the same JVM process; it registers
     Consumer callbacks via setEventListeners(...), so ChatServer has no compile-time dependency on ServerDashboard.
  • Both projects declare a class named Main (shown twice); they are in separate Maven projects.
endlegend

@enduml
